---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {REPO} from '../../scripts/catalog.mjs';
---
<Layout title="Contribute · Aha Looped Transformer"><div class="paper-page"><div class="la-eyebrow">COMMUNITY CONTRIBUTIONS</div><h1>One paper.<br/><em>Another perspective.</em></h1><p class="paper-summary">Help researchers find the next idea in recurrent computation. Add a work, share its implementation, or improve an existing entry.</p><div class="la-workflow"><span>01 · Submit a paper</span>→<span>02 · Metadata checks</span>→<span>03 · Maintainer review</span>→<span>04 · Published automatically</span></div><div class="la-detail"><h2>Share a work</h2><p>Bring an arXiv link, a short description in your own words, and any official code or weights. Sign in to GitHub to submit the form. The bot prepares a draft pull request; a maintainer checks the sources before publication.</p><div class="paper-links"><a class="button la-submit" href={`${REPO}/issues/new?template=submit-paper.yml`}>Open submission form ↗</a><a class="button" href={`${REPO}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>Contribute with a pull request ↗</a></div></div><section class="paper-note"><h2>What belongs here?</h2><p>Research on shared computation across depth, recurrent Transformer cores, adaptive recursion, and related latent reasoning methods. Include a source that explains the connection. Classifications can overlap; maintainers select the primary browsing category.</p><p>Use precise claims: independent parameters, effective depth and actual latency describe different things. Indicate unknown details and distinguish official releases from community implementations.</p></section><p>Submissions with missing metadata remain in review. Corrected and merged entries appear automatically on the collection, timeline, comparison view and their own paper page.</p></div></Layout>
